1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
Last time, she talked and the crew listened.

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:05,667
This time they answer.

3
00:00:06,117 --> 00:00:08,726
One answer got us a job.

4
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:12,220
Another would have hung up on her.

5
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:19,626
Every one of those is a single line in your file, and today you write them.

6
00:00:20,826 --> 00:00:25,174
An answer is a line that starts with a dash.

7
00:00:25,624 --> 00:00:29,102
Square brackets: the words Comms reads and picks.

8
00:00:29,552 --> 00:00:34,335
Round brackets, straight after, no space: where the conversation goes next.

9
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:39,133
Empty round brackets mean the call is over. Two rules.

10
00:00:39,583 --> 00:00:41,757
An answer is one line.

11
00:00:42,207 --> 00:00:50,033
And answers go at the end, below her last take, because that is when the crew gets them.

12
00:00:51,233 --> 00:00:57,320
Put a scene's key in the round brackets, and the call goes on there.

13
00:00:57,770 --> 00:00:59,943
So I need that scene.

14
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:04,307
Three hashes, a name, the key I just used.

15
00:01:04,757 --> 00:01:06,930
Speaker, her key. Two takes.

16
00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:09,989
And two answers of its own.

17
00:01:10,439 --> 00:01:13,917
Notice what is missing: no When, no Title.

18
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:17,411
Nothing places this scene as a call.

19
00:01:17,861 --> 00:01:22,209
The only way in is the answer that names it.

20
00:01:22,659 --> 00:01:26,572
And three hashes, like the first scene. Never four.

21
00:01:27,022 --> 00:01:30,500
A scene does not go inside another scene.

22
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:36,483
One more answer: the crew asks a question of their own.

23
00:01:36,933 --> 00:01:45,193
That goes to a scene where she tells them what she knows, and from there, on to the offer.

24
00:01:45,643 --> 00:01:48,687
Two answers lead to the same scene.

25
00:01:49,137 --> 00:01:50,441
That is fine.

26
00:01:50,891 --> 00:01:53,935
One limit: four answers in a scene.

27
00:01:54,385 --> 00:01:56,559
A fifth is never shown.

28
00:01:57,759 --> 00:02:00,802
So far an answer moves the conversation.

29
00:02:01,252 --> 00:02:03,861
Now one that changes the story.

30
00:02:04,311 --> 00:02:06,920
First the job she is offering.

31
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:10,413
Starts when revealed, so it is hidden.

32
00:02:10,863 --> 00:02:13,472
Done when thirty seconds. A reward.

33
00:02:13,922 --> 00:02:16,096
Now the answer. A semicolon.

34
00:02:16,546 --> 00:02:20,459
Everything after the semicolon is what the answer does.

35
00:02:20,909 --> 00:02:23,952
Accepts, and the key of the quest.

36
00:02:24,402 --> 00:02:26,576
The key, not the name.

37
00:02:27,026 --> 00:02:31,374
When Comms says we will tag her, the job starts.

38
00:02:32,574 --> 00:02:35,183
An answer can do two things.

39
00:02:35,633 --> 00:02:39,111
One semicolon, then a comma between the things.

40
00:02:39,561 --> 00:02:43,909
Not a second semicolon: that looks right and does nothing.

41
00:02:44,359 --> 00:02:50,011
The second thing here finishes the beat from last time, DS 1 Calls.

42
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:59,591
She has been answered, so that moment is over, and a finished beat shows up in the quest list as done.

43
00:03:00,041 --> 00:03:01,780
There are four words.

44
00:03:02,230 --> 00:03:03,970
Accepts starts a quest.

45
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:05,724
Completes finishes one.

46
00:03:06,174 --> 00:03:07,478
Fails fails one.

47
00:03:07,928 --> 00:03:14,885
Signal sends a word into the story, and any quest waiting on that word hears it.

48
00:03:16,085 --> 00:03:19,998
What the crew said should come back to them.

49
00:03:20,448 --> 00:03:23,926
When the job is done: then, reveal beacon_set.

50
00:03:24,376 --> 00:03:31,767
A beat, the same pattern as last time: starts when revealed, and its action places a call.

51
00:03:32,217 --> 00:03:33,522
And the scene.

52
00:03:33,972 --> 00:03:41,363
This one is a call of its own, so it has When hail and a Title again.

53
00:03:42,563 --> 00:03:44,737
Look at what you have.

54
00:03:45,187 --> 00:03:51,274
This answer is only offered to a crew that reported the hulk was cold.

55
00:03:51,724 --> 00:03:58,246
This one is only offered to a crew that took the job and finished it.

56
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:08,696
That is how you make an answer depend on the story: put it somewhere the crew can only reach when it is true.

57
00:04:09,146 --> 00:04:15,233
You will see another way in the documentation, the word if on the answer.

58
00:04:15,683 --> 00:04:18,726
Do not use it in this mission.

59
00:04:19,176 --> 00:04:27,872
It cannot read your quests or your credits, so the answer is never offered, and lint will not warn you.

60
00:04:28,322 --> 00:04:31,800
It comes into its own in Class 3.

61
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Lint. Clean.

62
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:37,493
A scene key that is not there.

63
00:04:37,943 --> 00:04:41,857
A word that is not one of the four.

64
00:04:42,307 --> 00:04:49,263
A quest key that is not there: the answer would end the call and start nothing.

65
00:04:49,713 --> 00:04:54,061
No round brackets: that line is no longer an answer.

66
00:04:54,511 --> 00:05:02,772
It is one more thing for her to say, and one day she would say it, brackets and all.

67
00:05:03,222 --> 00:05:11,048
And a scene with one hash too many, which takes the scene above it out of the game.

68
00:05:11,498 --> 00:05:14,107
Lint reads every one of these.

69
00:05:14,557 --> 00:05:21,948
What it cannot read is your intention: a job with no way to finish still lints clean.

70
00:05:23,148 --> 00:05:25,757
Her question, and my three answers.

71
00:05:26,207 --> 00:05:27,511
I ask first.

72
00:05:27,961 --> 00:05:30,570
Then I tell her. The offer.

73
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,759
We will tag her.

74
00:05:33,209 --> 00:05:37,122
Call over, and there is the job. Thirty seconds.

75
00:05:37,572 --> 00:05:40,615
Done, paid, and she is calling back.

76
00:05:41,065 --> 00:05:42,804
Now the other road.

77
00:05:43,254 --> 00:05:45,428
Find someone else. No job.

78
00:05:45,878 --> 00:05:48,052
And she does not call.

79
00:05:48,502 --> 00:05:50,676
Same file, two different evenings.

80
00:05:51,876 --> 00:05:54,920
You wrote a second call last time.

81
00:05:55,370 --> 00:06:03,196
Give it answers, and make one of them send a word into the story that finishes a quest.

82
00:06:03,646 --> 00:06:09,733
Next time: a job the crew can only get by picking up the call.
